)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ on the semicircle shown above." 13194139536155 true] [17592186386420 1113 #uuid "720aa004-4171-547e-b7da-98f76cf90612" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386420 1145 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(-1,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $y=\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =-2x \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta [\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ((-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{4}-{0}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{[-\\frac{{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta }{5}]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}({cos}^{5}⁡\\pi -{cos}^{5}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{8}{5\\pi }.\n$$" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386422 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386423 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386424 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386425 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386426 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1041 "selection" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386424 13194139536155 true] [17592186386421 1110 #uuid "5cd4a03d-aa52-53a9-8db2-911c87db0be8" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386422 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386422 1111 #uuid "c2c6e8a8-164f-55c1-8138-a11b93bb9a48" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386423 1034 "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386423 1111 #uuid "ce825d5c-4b2e-587e-acb6-cbfce522b867" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386424 1034 "\\frac{8}{5\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386424 1111 #uuid "80536cde-1922-59de-ab9d-88e0ad5e5062" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386425 1034 "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386425 1111 #uuid "d451367d-8e25-56d0-9000-933a0c1f1e39" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386426 1034 "\\frac{8\\pi }{5}" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386426 1111 #uuid "ccda1394-5b9c-540b-b6ca-a4a83d1ee0ef" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386428 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1089 "q-163279" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/719f86db69489f62bcbe2753e88cdc6713f04dc6f53415cc2484e2eaab8ffac3.png)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ on the semicircle shown above." 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1113 #uuid "22a142c9-9e75-53eb-93f7-728128a3ebf0" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386427 1145 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(0,1).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $x=\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2y-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }(2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}\\cdot 1=\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\n$$" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386429 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386430 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386431 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386432 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386433 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1041 "selection" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386431 13194139536155 true] [17592186386428 1110 #uuid "0745ff6a-c932-5b1d-99b3-a3b2405d2c6e" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386429 1034 "\\frac{5}{\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386429 1111 #uuid "9b3f5be0-7d2f-5927-9d74-21926d832708" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386430 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386430 1111 #uuid "cad94019-00dd-53ef-80fd-47a33542ca7a" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386431 1034 "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386431 1111 #uuid "c0863946-913f-5ca3-ac71-b8f4c9ad45d9" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386432 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386432 1111 #uuid "2bc94184-eea7-5d14-979d-70942aa37562" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386433 1034 "0" 13194139536155 true] [17592186386433 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536155 true] [17592186386433 1111 #uuid "9977d049-058f-561e-a2fc-77c1d66d1a61" 13194139536155 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-163070" 17592186386343 "q-163070/selection" 17592186386344 "q-163070/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" 17592186386345 "q-163070/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" 17592186386